      "result": "Exploring the workspace and Paris Open Data APIs to design an interactive Paris tree canopy explorer.\n\n\nChecking API capabilities and planning the app architecture for ~220k trees.\n\n\nCreating a data pipeline and building the application.\n\n\nBuilding the application UI and core components.\n\n\n**Canop\u00e9e de Paris** is in `/workspace/paris-trees` \u2014 an interactive atlas of the municipal tree canopy.\n\n### What you get\n- **Map** \u2014 MapLibre on a muted Carto basemap; **Supercluster** aggregation when zoomed out; individual markers when zoomed in; color by **genre** or **height**; gold **arbres remarquables** markers; arrondissement outlines.\n- **Filters** \u2014 Arrondissements 1er\u201320e, featured genera (Platanus, Aesculus, Tilia, Sophora, Celtis, \u2026), height/circumference ranges, remarkable-only toggle.\n- **Analytics** \u2014 Totals, diversity, mean/median height & circumference, genus bar chart, density per km\u00b2 by arrondissement (updates with filters).\n- **Remarkable showcase** \u2014 182 heritage trees with photos, criteria, planting age, pan-to-map.\n- **District comparison** \u2014 Stacked voirie vs parcs chart + comparison table with genus variety and density.\n- **Tree detail card** \u2014 French name, taxonomy, dimensions, stade, domaine, coordinates, heritage text/PDF when available.\n\n### Data\n~220k trees from Paris Open Data, preprocessed to `public/data/trees.json.gz` (~7.4 MB download). Sources are credited in the footer.\n\n### Run it\n```bash\ncd /workspace/paris-trees\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n```\n\nDev server: **http://localhost:5173/**\n\nRefresh data:\n```bash\nnpm run data:fetch\nnpm run data:build\n```\n\nFirst load parses the full inventory (brief loading screen); filtering and clustering then run in the browser on the active selection.",
